warning[ambiguous-precedence]: operator `|` has lower precedence than `&`
    ┌ test.idl:9:38
    │
  6 │ const long combined2 = (flags & MASK_LOWER);  // Simplified - comparison not supported
  7 │ const long combined3 = (base + offset) & ~(alignment - 1);
  8 │ 
  9 │ const long bad1 = MASK_LOWER & value | MASK_UPPER & value << 8;
    ·                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ ^ this operator has lower precedence
    ·                   └─ than this expression
 10 │ const long bad2 = flags & MASK_LOWER + 1;
 11 │ const long bad3 = base + offset & ~alignment - 1;
    └──
 help: add parentheses to clarify the intended order of operations

